    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Retirement is implemented. `bin/e2e` passes 3 of 4 tests: \"retire\", \"retire scenario 1\" and \"retire scenario 2\" pass, and \"retire scenario 3\" fails. I think that failure comes from a conflict between the test's reload helper and the change request, not from a bug in the app.\n\n**Why scenario 3 fails**\n- Vic's screen is showing Ben. Then Uma retires Ben from 2026-03-15, and the test calls `ui.refresh(pg_vic)` with \"show retired\" still off on Vic's screen (`acceptance.spec.ts:429`).\n- `refresh` in `e2e/support/ui.ts:121` waits for every person row that was on screen before the reload to come back.\n- The request says retired people have \"no row \u2026 on the screen at all\" unless \"show retired\" is on, and a reload must show what the store holds now. So Ben's row correctly goes away, and the helper times out waiting for it (\"the sheet is back on screen after a reload\").\n- Ada and Cam aren't retired, and their claim counts only go up, so Ben is the only row that can be missing.\n- The only way to pass would be to keep showing someone on a screen after another user retired them. That contradicts the request, so I didn't build it. I couldn't fix the helper either, because `e2e/support/` and the spec are off-limits.\n\n**What was built**\n- **Stored data:** a new migration, `V17__person_retired.sql`, adds a `retired_from` date to each person. It is empty while they aren't retired.\n- **Server:**\n  - `POST /api/sheets/{id}/people/{personId}/retire` sets the date, using the sheet's today if none is given.\n  - It writes `PERSON_RETIRED sheet=\u2026 by=\u2026 name=\u2026 from=\u2026` to the audit file.\n  - The people list now includes `retiredFrom`.\n- **Claim rule:** a claim dated after the person's retirement date is refused when it's added, edited or quick-added, with nothing written. The server answers 422. Claims dated on or before the date are still allowed.\n- **Screen:**\n  - Each person's row shows `person-retired` (yes/no) and `person-retired-from`, plus a date box (`person-retire-date`) and a Retire button (`person-retire`). If retiring fails, the error appears in `person-error`.\n  - A `show-retired` checkbox is off when the screen first opens and stays as it is when a sheet is loaded. When it's off, retired people get no row at all.\n  - All totals still count everyone's claims, retired or not.\n  - A refused claim shows an error in the claim form or the quick-add box.\n\nTo get scenario 3 passing, someone allowed to change the tests would need to fix `refresh`, so that a row legitimately disappearing after a reload doesn't count as a failure, or change the scenario to turn \"show retired\" on before Vic's reload. Tell me if you'd rather have a workaround in the app instead.",
